{"authored" [{"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "96b3c950dde71577c2afac8d52c6a48bf7dc78542d6bc2bc6a74fa9e2099e0bc" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/state.json" "file_sha256" "6cdf3b096f6c85db5dc278d862a4ca6c8b73e3a38dc02891eb5ec955ebfe6b82" "basis" 1196 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/d1d49c23cebfe2979c8bff7b7f19d5435807a8d1aec348070aadfab1e9d2ca19.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-10457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (5{cos}^{2}⁡2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-10457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{cos}^{2}⁡2x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int [5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-10457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2d097bc9bebb8d0c149fdb91ae88fc5bb4c8f339de3a2dc0a9341278d327f3"} {"question" "q-10457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-10457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-10457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{5x}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int [1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2d097bc9bebb8d0c149fdb91ae88fc5bb4c8f339de3a2dc0a9341278d327f3"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] ["math" "x-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-114709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/assets/86e34aa6aff8f62f1913d2f432f1236d651d3813647e512d398b51c7b7ce48f7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)+{x}^{2}+4,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)+{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x=2{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)+{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+{x}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{{0}^{3}}{3}+4\\cdot 0] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}+2\\pi ]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}+2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348729" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2d097bc9bebb8d0c149fdb91ae88fc5bb4c8f339de3a2dc0a9341278d327f3"} {"question" "q-348729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348729" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi^3}{24}+2\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2d097bc9bebb8d0c149fdb91ae88fc5bb4c8f339de3a2dc0a9341278d327f3"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/assets/d1d49c23cebfe2979c8bff7b7f19d5435807a8d1aec348070aadfab1e9d2ca19.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y={x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1)=-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{(\\pi /2)^{3}}{3}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{24}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8b2d097bc9bebb8d0c149fdb91ae88fc5bb4c8f339de3a2dc0a9341278d327f3"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"} {"question" "q-348886" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7\\pi^3}{24}-\\frac{\\pi}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044295/state.json" "file_sha256" "82d9e1e406e90feffd3f38eb9a9ac2dddde30ab27380b2a90205fec4a4e09e5f"}] "usage" {"q-114709" [] "q-3